/-!
# The local Lefschetz number of a coefficient complex on a scheme over a finite field

Let `k` be a finite field with `p ^ q` elements, let `k̄` be an algebraically closed extension of
`k`, let `X` be a scheme over `k` and let `Λ` be a finite coefficient ring.  The local Lefschetz
number of an object `K` of `D_ctf(X_étale, Λ)` is the sum

`∑_{x ∈ X(k)} Tr(π_x | K_x̄)`

over the `k`-rational points of `X`, of the traces of the geometric Frobenius of
[Stacks, Tag 03SW] acting on the stalk of `K` at the geometric point `x̄` above `x`.  Every
ingredient of that sum is read off the geometry: `X(k)` is the set of sections of the structure
morphism, `K_x̄` is the derived étale stalk of `K` at `x̄`, and `π_x` is the action of the inverse
of the arithmetic Frobenius of `k̄` over `k`.

Perfection of `K_x̄`, which is what makes the trace defined, is *proved* here and not assumed:
`AlgebraicGeometry.derivedEtaleModuleStalk_isPerfect_of_isRepresentedByConstructibleFlatComplex`
is the statement that the derived stalk of an object of `D_ctf(X_étale, Λ)` is a perfect object
of `D(Λ)`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.rationalPointFrobeniusStalkFunctor` — the geometric Frobenius `π_x` of
  [Stacks, Tag 03SW] as an endomorphism of the stalk functor of the *bounded* small étale site,
  transported from Mathlib's small étale site across the comparison
  `AlgebraicGeometry.sheafEquivCompSheafFiberIso`.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.rationalPointFrobeniusStalkComplex` — the induced endomorphism `π_x`
  of the stalk complex of a cochain complex of coefficient sheaves, degreewise.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.ctfStalkDatum` — the stalks `K_x̄` at the geometric points above the
  rational points, *with their perfection derived*, together with the Frobenius actions on them.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.localLefschetzNumberOfCtf` — **the local Lefschetz number of `K`**,
  [Stacks, Tag 03TY] for an object of `D_ctf(X_étale, Λ)` on an actual scheme over an actual
  finite field.

## Main results

* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.localLefschetzNumberOfCtf_eq_sum` — the local Lefschetz number is the
  sum over `X(k)` of the traces of `π_x` on `K_x̄`.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.derivedRationalPointFrobenius_app_Q` — on the class of a cochain
  complex of coefficient sheaves the Frobenius action on the derived stalk is the degreewise
  geometric Frobenius of the stalk complex.

## Implementation notes

**How membership of `D_ctf(X, Λ)` is written.**  The source takes `K ∈ D_ctf(X, Λ)` and appeals,
for perfection of the stalks, to [Stacks, Tag 03TT]: on a quasi-compact and quasi-separated
scheme, an object of `D(X_étale, Λ)` lies in `D_ctf(X_étale, Λ)` — condition (1) — exactly when
it is represented by a bounded complex of constructible flat sheaves of `Λ`-modules —
condition (2).  Condition (2) is the form used here,
`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.IsRepresentedByConstructibleFlatComplex`; it is also how
[SGA 4½, Rapport 4.6] *defines* `D_ctf`.

That is the formulation the source's own hypotheses on `Λ` demand.  Tag 03TX, whose setting
Tag 03TY inherits, takes `Λ` to be a finite ring, and the section the trace material runs in,
Tag 03SZ, fixes a finite ring `Λ` of cardinality prime to `p` whose typical example is the group
ring `(ℤ/ℓ^nℤ)[G]` of a finite group — noncommutative as soon as `G` is — takes all `Λ`-modules
to be left modules, and sets `Λ^natural` to be the quotient of `Λ` by the additive subgroup
generated by its commutators, which is a proper quotient exactly in the noncommutative case.
Condition (2) is a condition on left `Λ`-modules in which no product of two scalars is taken:
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsConstructibleFlatModuleSheaf` is stratumwise local constancy with finite
projective values, and the route from it to perfection of the stalks —
`AlgebraicGeometry.etaleModuleStalk_projective_of_isConstructibleFlatModuleSheaf`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.stalk_finite` and the additive-functor bookkeeping of
`AlgebraicGeometry.stalk_isPerfect_of_finite_projective` — is available over an arbitrary ring.
Condition (1) read literally is not: this development's
`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.ConstructibleFiniteTorDerivedCategory` measures Tor dimension against
derived tensor products on the slices of the constant coefficient ringed site of
[Stacks, Tag 03TR], and `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite` has a structure sheaf valued in
`CommRingCat`, so condition (1) is formed only for a commutative `Λ`.  The same goes for the
other route to perfection of a stalk, `AlgebraicGeometry.stalk_isPerfect`, which derives finite
projectivity from flatness over that ring sheaf: Mathlib's `Module.Flat` is available over a
commutative ring only, and `Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsFlat` is exactness of a tensor product of
sheaves of modules.

**The stalks and the Frobenius are computed from `K` and `X`.**  The étale stalk at a geometric
point is exact, so it induces a functor on unbounded derived categories,
`AlgebraicGeometry.derivedEtaleModuleStalkFunctor`, and the Frobenius, being a natural
endomorphism of the stalk functor, induces one of the derived stalk functor,
`AlgebraicGeometry.derivedEtaleModuleStalkEndo`.  Both are applied to the object `K` itself;
nothing about its stalks or about the action on them is postulated.  The general shape of the
definition, for an arbitrary finite ring and arbitrary perfect stalks with arbitrary
endomorphisms, is `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.localLefschetzNumber`, of which this is the geometric
instance.

**Two presentations of the small étale site.**  Constructible flatness and the stalk functor that
`AlgebraicGeometry.stalk_isPerfect_of_isConstructibleFlatModuleSheaf` is stated for live on the
bounded small étale site `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale B X.obj X.property`, whereas the geometric
Frobenius `Stacks.Frobenius.geometricFrobeniusStalkFunctor` of Tag 03SW lives on Mathlib's
`Scheme.Etale`.  The two are identified by `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.sheafEquiv`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.sheafEquivCompSheafFiberIso` identifies the two stalk functors at a geometric
point; conjugating the Frobenius by that isomorphism carries it to the bounded site, where the
perfection theorem applies to the same object.

**Finiteness of `X(k)`.**  The sum is over `X(k)`, so `X(k)` must be finite; this is carried as a
`Fintype` instance, as in
`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.compactSupportLefschetzNumber_eq_localLefschetzNumber`.  It is a property
of `X` and `k` and not of the coefficient object, so it does not stand for anything the tag
derives from `K`.

**The scheme.**  Tag 03TX, whose setting Tag 03TY inherits, takes `X` to be a projective curve
over the finite field `k`; the `X` here is an arbitrary scheme of the big étale site with a
morphism to `Spec k` and finitely many `k`-rational points.  That is a generalisation and not a
restriction — a projective curve over `k` is quasi-compact and quasi-separated and has finitely
many `k`-rational points — so nothing about the source's `X` is imposed.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03TY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03TY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03TX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03TX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03TT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03TT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03TR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03TR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03SZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03SZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03SW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03SW)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry

universe u w r

namespace Stacks.EtaleCohomology

variable (B : BigEtaleSite.{u}) (X : B.Scheme) (Λ : Type r) [Ring Λ]
  [∀ (S T : B.Scheme) (g : T ⟶ S),
    ((AlgebraicGeometry.smallEtaleBaseChange B g).sheafPushforwardContinuous (ModuleCat.{w} Λ)
      (SmallEtale.topology B S.obj S.property)
      (SmallEtale.topology B T.obj T.property)).IsRightAdjoint]
  [∀ (T : B.Scheme) (V : SmallEtale B T.obj T.property),
    HasWeakSheafify ((SmallEtale.topology B T.obj T.property).over V) (ModuleCat.{w} Λ)]
  [HasColimitsOfSize.{u, u} (ModuleCat.{w} Λ)]
  [HasSheafify (SmallEtale.topology B X.obj X.property) (ModuleCat.{w} Λ)]
  [AB5OfSize.{u, u} (ModuleCat.{w} Λ)]
  [HasLimitsOfSize.{u, u} (ModuleCat.{w} Λ)]
  {k : Type u} [Field k] [Fintype k] (kbar : Type u) [Field kbar] [IsAlgClosed kbar]
  [Algebra k kbar] (p q : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] [CharP kbar p]

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

/-! ### The geometric Frobenius on the stalk of the bounded small étale site -/

/-- **The geometric Frobenius `π_x` of [Stacks, Tag 03SW]** at a `k`-rational point `x`, as an
endomorphism of the stalk functor of the bounded small étale site at the geometric point `x̄`
above `x`.  It is `Stacks.Frobenius.geometricFrobeniusStalkFunctor` conjugated by the comparison
`AlgebraicGeometry.sheafEquivCompSheafFiberIso` of the stalk functors of the two presentations of
the small étale site. -/
@[sga "4½ Rapport 1.5" "more general"]
public def rationalPointFrobeniusStalkFunctor (hcard : Fintype.card k = p ^ q)
    (x : Spec (.of k) ⟶ X.obj) :
    etaleModuleStalkFunctor.{u, w, r} B X Λ (Stacks.Frobenius.rationalGeometricPoint kbar x) ⟶
      etaleModuleStalkFunctor.{u, w, r} B X Λ
        (Stacks.Frobenius.rationalGeometricPoint kbar x) :=
  (sheafEquivCompSheafFiberIso.{u, w, r} B X Λ
      (Stacks.Frobenius.rationalGeometricPoint kbar x)).inv ≫
    Functor.whiskerLeft (SmallEtale.sheafEquiv B X.obj X.property (ModuleCat.{w} Λ)).functor
      (Stacks.Frobenius.geometricFrobeniusStalkFunctor (ModuleCat.{w} Λ) kbar p q hcard x) ≫
    (sheafEquivCompSheafFiberIso.{u, w, r} B X Λ
      (Stacks.Frobenius.rationalGeometricPoint kbar x)).hom

/-- **The endomorphism `π_x` of the stalk complex of a cochain complex of coefficient sheaves**:
the geometric Frobenius of [Stacks, Tag 03SW] applied degreewise.  It commutes with the
differentials because the Frobenius is a natural transformation of the stalk functor. -/
@[sga "4½ Rapport 1.5" "more general"]
public def rationalPointFrobeniusStalkComplex (hcard : Fintype.card k = p ^ q)
    (x : Spec (.of k) ⟶ X.obj)
    (K : CochainComplex
      (Sheaf (SmallEtale.topology B X.obj X.property) (ModuleCat.{w} Λ)) ℤ) :
    etaleModuleStalkComplex B X Λ (Stacks.Frobenius.rationalGeometricPoint kbar x) K ⟶
      etaleModuleStalkComplex B X Λ (Stacks.Frobenius.rationalGeometricPoint kbar x) K :=
  (NatTrans.mapHomologicalComplex
    (rationalPointFrobeniusStalkFunctor.{u, w, r} B X Λ kbar p q hcard x)
    (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).app K

/-- **The Frobenius `π_x` acting on the derived stalk `K_x̄`**, for an object `K` of
`D(X_étale, Λ)`: the endomorphism of the derived stalk functor induced by the geometric Frobenius
of [Stacks, Tag 03SW]. -/
@[sga "4½ Rapport 1.5" "more general"]
public def derivedRationalPointFrobenius (hcard : Fintype.card k = p ^ q)
    (x : Spec (.of k) ⟶ X.obj) :
    derivedEtaleModuleStalkFunctor B X Λ (Stacks.Frobenius.rationalGeometricPoint kbar x) ⟶
      derivedEtaleModuleStalkFunctor B X Λ
        (Stacks.Frobenius.rationalGeometricPoint kbar x) :=
  derivedEtaleModuleStalkEndo B X Λ (Stacks.Frobenius.rationalGeometricPoint kbar x)
    (rationalPointFrobeniusStalkFunctor.{u, w, r} B X Λ kbar p q hcard x)

/-- On the class of a cochain complex of coefficient sheaves the Frobenius action on the derived
stalk is the degreewise geometric Frobenius of the stalk complex. -/
public theorem derivedRationalPointFrobenius_app_Q (hcard : Fintype.card k = p ^ q)
    (x : Spec (.of k) ⟶ X.obj)
    (K : CochainComplex
      (Sheaf (SmallEtale.topology B X.obj X.property) (ModuleCat.{w} Λ)) ℤ) :
    (derivedRationalPointFrobenius.{u, w, r} B X Λ kbar p q hcard x).app
        (DerivedCategory.Q.obj K) =
      (derivedEtaleModuleStalkObjQIso B X Λ
          (Stacks.Frobenius.rationalGeometricPoint kbar x) K).hom ≫
        DerivedCategory.Q.map
          (rationalPointFrobeniusStalkComplex.{u, w, r} B X Λ kbar p q hcard x K) ≫
        (derivedEtaleModuleStalkObjQIso B X Λ
          (Stacks.Frobenius.rationalGeometricPoint kbar x) K).inv :=
  derivedEtaleModuleStalkEndo_app_Q B X Λ _ _ K

/-! ### The local Lefschetz number -/

variable [Finite Λ]

/-- **The stalks `K_x̄` with the Frobenius acting on them**, for an object `K` of
`D_ctf(X_étale, Λ)` and the geometric points above the `k`-rational points of `X`.

Both ingredients are computed from `K` and `X`: the stalk is the derived étale stalk of `K` at
the geometric point above `x`, and the endomorphism is the geometric Frobenius `π_x` of
[Stacks, Tag 03SW] acting on it.  Perfection of each stalk is *derived*, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.derivedEtaleModuleStalk_isPerfect_of_isRepresentedByConstructibleFlatComplex`,
and not supplied: that is what the source reads off membership of `D_ctf(X, Λ)` through
[Stacks, Tag 03TT]. -/
public def ctfStalkDatum (hcard : Fintype.card k = p ^ q)
    (f : X.obj ⟶ Spec (.of k))
    (K : DerivedCategory
      (Sheaf (SmallEtale.topology B X.obj X.property) (ModuleCat.{w} Λ)))
    (hK : IsRepresentedByConstructibleFlatComplex.{u, w, r} B X Λ K) :
    FrobeniusActionOnStalks.{r, w, u} Λ (rationalPoints f) where
  stalk x :=
    ⟨(derivedEtaleModuleStalkFunctor B X Λ
        (Stacks.Frobenius.rationalGeometricPoint kbar x.1)).obj K,
      derivedEtaleModuleStalk_isPerfect_of_isRepresentedByConstructibleFlatComplex
        B X Λ K hK _⟩
  frobeniusAction x :=
    (derivedRationalPointFrobenius.{u, w, r} B X Λ kbar p q hcard x.1).app K

/-- **Stacks, Tag 03TY: the local Lefschetz number of `K`.**  For a finite field `k` with `p ^ q`
elements, an algebraically closed extension `k̄` of `k`, a scheme `X` over `k` with structure
morphism `f` and finitely many `k`-rational points, an arbitrary finite — possibly
noncommutative — coefficient ring `Λ`, and an object `K` of `D_ctf(X_étale, Λ)`, this is the sum

`∑_{x ∈ X(k)} Tr(π_x | K_x̄)`

over the `k`-rational points of `X` of the traces of the geometric Frobenius `π_x` of
[Stacks, Tag 03SW] on the derived stalk `K_x̄` of `K` at the geometric point above `x`, an element
of the additive commutator quotient `Λ^natural`.

Perfection of each stalk `K_x̄`, which the source reads off `K ∈ D_ctf(X, Λ)` through
[Stacks, Tag 03TT], is proved here rather than supplied:  it is
`AlgebraicGeometry.derivedEtaleModuleStalk_isPerfect_of_isRepresentedByConstructibleFlatComplex`.
Membership of `D_ctf(X, Λ)` is written as condition (2) of [Stacks, Tag 03TT], the condition that
`K` be represented by a bounded complex of constructible flat sheaves of `Λ`-modules, which is
also how [SGA 4½, Rapport 4.6] defines `D_ctf`; see the implementation notes of this file for why
that is the formulation the source's generality on `Λ` calls for. -/
@[stacks 03TY "the local Lefschetz number of an object K of D_ctf(X_étale, Λ) on a scheme X over \
a finite field k: the sum over the k-rational points x of X of the traces of the geometric \
Frobenius π_x of 03SW on the stalk K_x̄, an element of the additive commutator quotient \
Λ^natural. Λ is the arbitrary finite, possibly noncommutative, ring of 03TX and 03SZ. X(k), the \
stalks K_x̄ and the actions π_x are all computed from K and X — K_x̄ is the derived étale stalk \
of K at the geometric point above x and π_x is the induced action of the geometric Frobenius — \
and perfection of each K_x̄ is derived from membership of D_ctf, as in the source. Membership of \
D_ctf(X_étale, Λ) is written as condition (2) of 03TT, that K be represented by a bounded \
complex of constructible flat sheaves of Λ-modules, which is also how SGA 4½ Rapport 4.6 defines \
D_ctf",
  sga "4½ Rapport 4.6" "D_ctf(X, Λ)"]
public def localLefschetzNumberOfCtf (hcard : Fintype.card k = p ^ q)
    (f : X.obj ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [Fintype (rationalPoints f)]
    (K : DerivedCategory
      (Sheaf (SmallEtale.topology B X.obj X.property) (ModuleCat.{w} Λ)))
    (hK : IsRepresentedByConstructibleFlatComplex.{u, w, r} B X Λ K) :
    CategoryTheory.FilteredDerived.AdditiveCommutatorQuotient Λ :=
  localLefschetzNumber Λ (rationalPoints f)
    (ctfStalkDatum.{u, w, r} B X Λ kbar p q hcard f K hK)

/-- The local Lefschetz number of `K` is the sum over the `k`-rational points `x` of `X` of the
traces of the geometric Frobenius `π_x` on the derived stalks `K_x̄`. -/
public theorem localLefschetzNumberOfCtf_eq_sum (hcard : Fintype.card k = p ^ q)
    (f : X.obj ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [Fintype (rationalPoints f)]
    (K : DerivedCategory
      (Sheaf (SmallEtale.topology B X.obj X.property) (ModuleCat.{w} Λ)))
    (hK : IsRepresentedByConstructibleFlatComplex.{u, w, r} B X Λ K) :
    localLefschetzNumberOfCtf.{u, w, r} B X Λ kbar p q hcard f K hK =
      ∑ x : rationalPoints f, CategoryTheory.FilteredDerived.perfectDerivedTrace Λ
        ⟨(derivedEtaleModuleStalkFunctor B X Λ
            (Stacks.Frobenius.rationalGeometricPoint kbar x.1)).obj K,
          derivedEtaleModuleStalk_isPerfect_of_isRepresentedByConstructibleFlatComplex
            B X Λ K hK _⟩
        ((derivedRationalPointFrobenius.{u, w, r} B X Λ kbar p q hcard x.1).app K) :=
  rfl

end Stacks.EtaleCohomology

end
